    "title": "East Blaine de-annexation to go before city voters - NewsBreak",
    "text": "thenorthernlight.com\nwebsite\nBlaine\nEast Blaine de-annexation to go before city voters\nBy Grace McCarthy,\n5 hours agoCity of Blaine residents will soon decide whether they would like to de-annex a chunk of east Blaine, which would likely lead to high-density housing near Semiahmoo. Blaine City Council unanimously voted 6-0 during its Blaine City Council meeting on July 14 to place a ballot measure in the November 4 election that will allow city voters to decide if they want to de-annex 573 acres of incorporated urban growth area (UGA) in east Blaine, 473 of which is the Grandis Pond property. The land size was previously estimated to be 552 acres.",
